G4671.b:
⟪αὐτός⟫, -ή, -ό, determinative pron., in late Gk. much more freq. than in cl. (WM, 178 f.; Jannaris, HGG, §1399).
⟪1.⟫ Emphatic (so always in nom. exc. when preceded by the art., v. infr., iii);
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪self⟫ (ipse), expressing opposition, distinction, exclusion, etc., αὐ. ἐκχυθήσεται, ⟦Luke 5:37|Lk 5:37⟧; αὐ. ἐγινώσκεν, ⟦John 2:25|Jo 2:25⟧; αὐ. ὑμεῖς, ⟦John 3:28|Jo 3:28⟧; καὶ αὐ. ἐγώ, ⟦Romans 15:14|Ro 15:14⟧; αὐ. Ἰησοῦς, ⟦John 2:24|Jo 2:24⟧; αὐ. καὶ οἱ μετ’ αὐτοῦ, ⟦Matthew 2:25|Mk 2:25⟧; ὑμεῖς αὐ., ⟦Mark 6:31|Mk 6:31⟧; esp. (as freq in cl.) αὐ. ὁ, ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧, ⟦Mark 6:17|Mk 6:17⟧, ⟦John 16:27|Jo 16:27⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:11|I Th 3:11⟧, al.; in late Gk., sometimes weakened, ἐν αὐτῇ τ. ὥρᾳ, ⟪in that hour⟫, ⟦Luke 10:21|Lk 10:21⟧ (M, Pr., 91; MM, s.v.);
	⟪(2)⟫ emphatic, ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫ (M, Pr., 86; Bl., § 48, 1, 2, 7), ⟦Matthew 1:21|Mt 1:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:50|12:50⟧, ⟦Luke 6:35|Lk 6:35⟧, al.; pointing to some one as master (cl.), ⟦Matthew 8:24|Mt 8:24⟧, ⟦Mark 4:38|Mk 4:38⟧, al.; αὐ., καὶ αὐ. = οὗτος, ὁ δε (Bl., § 48, 1), ⟦Matthew 14:2|Mt 14:2⟧, ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦Mark 14:44|44⟧, ⟦Luke 1:22|Lk 1:22⟧ ⟦Luke 2:28|2:28⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ In oblique cases (cl.), for the simple pron. of 3rd pers., ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫, ⟦Matthew 7:9|Mt 7:9⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:12|10:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:44|26:44⟧, al.; with ptcp. in gen. absol., ⟦Matthew 9:18|Mt 9:18⟧, ⟦Mark 13:1|Mk 13:1⟧, al. (for irreg. constructions, V. Bl., § 74, 5); pleonastically after the relative (cf. Heb. ⁨אֲשֶׁר לֹו⁩; WM, 184 ff.; Bl., § 50, 4; MM, s.v.), ⟦Mark 7:25|Mk 7:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:8|Re 3:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:2|7:2⟧, al.; in constr. ad sensum, without proper subject expressly indicated, ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 8:5|Ac 8:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:13|II Co 2:13⟧, al.; gen. αὐτοῦ = ἐκείνου, ⟦Romans 11:11|Ro 11:11⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦Titus 3:5|Tit 3:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:4|He 2:4⟧.
⟪3.⟫ ὁ, ἡ, τὸ αὐ., ⟪the same⟫: ⟦Hebrews 1:12|He 1:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:8|13:8⟧; τὸ αὐ., ποιεῖν, ⟦Matthew 5:46|Mt 5:46⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:47|47⟧, al.; φρονεῖν, ⟦Romans 12:16|Ro 12:16⟧ ⟦Romans 15:5|15:5⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:2|Phl 2:2⟧, al.; τὰ αὐ., ⟦Acts 15:27|Ac 15:27⟧, ⟦Romans 2:1|Ro 2:1⟧, al.; κατὰ τὸ (τὰ) αὐ. (MM, s.v.), ⟦Acts 14:1|Ac 14:1⟧, ⟦Luke 6:23|Lk 6:23⟧, al.; ἐπὶ τὸ αὐ., ⟪together⟫ (MM, s.v.), ⟦Matthew 22:34|Mt 22:34⟧, ⟦Acts 1:15|Ac 1:15⟧, al.; ἓν κ. τὸ αὐ., ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|12:11⟧; c. dat. (cl.), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧; with a noun, λόγος, Mk 14:39; μέτρος, ⟦Philippians 1:30|Phl 1:30⟧; πνεῦμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:4|I Co 12:4⟧.

G4675.b:
⟪αὐτός⟫, -ή, -ό, determinative pron., in late Gk. much more freq. than in cl. (WM, 178 f.; Jannaris, HGG, §1399).
⟪1.⟫ Emphatic (so always in nom. exc. when preceded by the art., v. infr., iii);
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪self⟫ (ipse), expressing opposition, distinction, exclusion, etc., αὐ. ἐκχυθήσεται, ⟦Luke 5:37|Lk 5:37⟧; αὐ. ἐγινώσκεν, ⟦John 2:25|Jo 2:25⟧; αὐ. ὑμεῖς, ⟦John 3:28|Jo 3:28⟧; καὶ αὐ. ἐγώ, ⟦Romans 15:14|Ro 15:14⟧; αὐ. Ἰησοῦς, ⟦John 2:24|Jo 2:24⟧; αὐ. καὶ οἱ μετ’ αὐτοῦ, ⟦Matthew 2:25|Mk 2:25⟧; ὑμεῖς αὐ., ⟦Mark 6:31|Mk 6:31⟧; esp. (as freq in cl.) αὐ. ὁ, ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧, ⟦Mark 6:17|Mk 6:17⟧, ⟦John 16:27|Jo 16:27⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:11|I Th 3:11⟧, al.; in late Gk., sometimes weakened, ἐν αὐτῇ τ. ὥρᾳ, ⟪in that hour⟫, ⟦Luke 10:21|Lk 10:21⟧ (M, Pr., 91; MM, s.v.);
	⟪(2)⟫ emphatic, ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫ (M, Pr., 86; Bl., § 48, 1, 2, 7), ⟦Matthew 1:21|Mt 1:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:50|12:50⟧, ⟦Luke 6:35|Lk 6:35⟧, al.; pointing to some one as master (cl.), ⟦Matthew 8:24|Mt 8:24⟧, ⟦Mark 4:38|Mk 4:38⟧, al.; αὐ., καὶ αὐ. = οὗτος, ὁ δε (Bl., § 48, 1), ⟦Matthew 14:2|Mt 14:2⟧, ⟦Mark 14:15|Mk 14:15⟧, ⟦Mark 14:44|44⟧, ⟦Luke 1:22|Lk 1:22⟧ ⟦Luke 2:28|2:28⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ In oblique cases (cl.), for the simple pron. of 3rd pers., ⟪he⟫, ⟪she⟫, ⟪it⟫, ⟦Matthew 7:9|Mt 7:9⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:12|10:12⟧, ⟦Matthew 26:44|26:44⟧, al.; with ptcp. in gen. absol., ⟦Matthew 9:18|Mt 9:18⟧, ⟦Mark 13:1|Mk 13:1⟧, al. (for irreg. constructions, V. Bl., § 74, 5); pleonastically after the relative (cf. Heb. ⁨אֲשֶׁר לֹו⁩; WM, 184 ff.; Bl., § 50, 4; MM, s.v.), ⟦Mark 7:25|Mk 7:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:8|Re 3:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:2|7:2⟧, al.; in constr. ad sensum, without proper subject expressly indicated, ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 8:5|Ac 8:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:13|II Co 2:13⟧, al.; gen. αὐτοῦ = ἐκείνου, ⟦Romans 11:11|Ro 11:11⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦Titus 3:5|Tit 3:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:4|He 2:4⟧.
⟪3.⟫ ὁ, ἡ, τὸ αὐ., ⟪the same⟫: ⟦Hebrews 1:12|He 1:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:8|13:8⟧; τὸ αὐ., ποιεῖν, ⟦Matthew 5:46|Mt 5:46⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:47|47⟧, al.; φρονεῖν, ⟦Romans 12:16|Ro 12:16⟧ ⟦Romans 15:5|15:5⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:2|Phl 2:2⟧, al.; τὰ αὐ., ⟦Acts 15:27|Ac 15:27⟧, ⟦Romans 2:1|Ro 2:1⟧, al.; κατὰ τὸ (τὰ) αὐ. (MM, s.v.), ⟦Acts 14:1|Ac 14:1⟧, ⟦Luke 6:23|Lk 6:23⟧, al.; ἐπὶ τὸ αὐ., ⟪together⟫ (MM, s.v.), ⟦Matthew 22:34|Mt 22:34⟧, ⟦Acts 1:15|Ac 1:15⟧, al.; ἓν κ. τὸ αὐ., ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|12:11⟧; c. dat. (cl.), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:5|I Co 11:5⟧; with a noun, λόγος, Mk 14:39; μέτρος, ⟦Philippians 1:30|Phl 1:30⟧; πνεῦμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:4|I Co 12:4⟧.

G4606.b:
⟪Σιδώνιος⟫, -α, -ον
(< Σιδών), ⟪of Sidon, Sidonian⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ the region: sc. χώρα, ⟦Luke 4:26|Lk 4:26⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ the people: ⟦Acts 12:20|Ac 12:20⟧.†

G4616.b:
⟪σινδών⟫, -όνος, ἡ
[in LXX: ⟦Judges 14:12|Jg 14:12, 13A⟧, ⟦Proverbs 31:24|Pr 31:24⟧ (⁨סָדִין⁩), I Mac 10:64 A * ;] ⟪fine linen cloth⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ as used for swathing dead bodies (cf. Hdt., ii, 86): ⟦Matthew 27:59|Mt 27:59⟧, ⟦Mark 15:46|Mk 15:46⟧, ⟦Luke 23:53|Lk 23:53⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ a garment or wrap of this material (cf. ICC, ⟦Judges 14:12|Jg, l.c.⟧): ⟦Mark 14:51|Mk 14:51, 52⟧.†

G4622.b:
⟪Σιών⟫ indecl., in NT anarth., but in LXX when used of the city of Jerusalem, ἡ Σ.
(Heb. ⁨צִיּוֹן⁩), ⟪Zion⟫;
⟪1.⟫ the mountain: in typical sense, of the Church, ⟦Hebrews 12:22|He 12:22⟧; of heaven, ⟦Revelation 14:1|Re 14:1⟧.
⟪2.⟫ The city, i.e. Jerusalem; in poetical sense;
⟪(a)⟫ of the inhabitants: θυγάτηρ Σ, ⟦Matthew 21:5|Mt 21:5⟧, ⟦John 12:15|Jo 12:15⟧ (LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ in wider sense, of Israel: ⟦Romans 11:26|Ro 11:26⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ fig.: τίθήμι ἐν Σ λίθον, ⟦Romans 9:33|Ro 9:33⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:6|I Pe 2:6⟧ (LXX).†

G4625.b:
† ⟪σκάνδαλον⟫, -ου, τό
(late form of the rare word σκανδάληθρον, v. LS, s.v.) [in LXX chiefly for ⁨מוֹקֵשׁ⁩, ⁨מִכְשׁוֹל⁩ ;] prop., the ⟪bait-stick⟫ of a trap, ⟪a snare, stumbling-block⟫ (⟦Leviticus 19:14|Le 19:14⟧, Jth 5:1): fig., ⟦Romans 9:33|Ro 9:33⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:8|I Pe 2:8⟧ (⟦Isaiah 8:14|Is 8:14⟧; aliter in LXX; στερεὸν σκανδάλου in Aq.). Metaph., of that which causes error or sin;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons: ⟦Matthew 13:41|Mt 13:41⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:23|16:23⟧; Χριστὸς ἐσταυρωμένος, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:23|I Co 1:23⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of things: ⟦Matthew 18:7|Mt 18:7⟧, ⟦Romans 11:9|Ro 11:9⟧ (LXX) ⟦Romans 14:13|14:13⟧, ⟦1 John 2:10|I Jo 2:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 2:14|Re 2:14⟧; τὸ σ. τοῦ σταυροῦ, ⟦Galatians 5:11|Ga 5:11⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 18:7|Mt 18:7⟧, ⟦Luke 17:1|Lk 17:1⟧, ⟦Romans 16:17|Ro 16:17⟧.†
SYN.: πρόσκομμα

G4642.b:
⟪σκληρός⟫, -ά, -όν
(< σκέλλω, ⟪to dry⟫), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨קָשָׁה⁩ ;] ⟪hard⟫ to the touch, ⟪rough, harsh⟫, (opp. to μαλακός); metaph., in various uses;
⟪(a)⟫ of men, ⟪hard, stern, severe⟫: ⟦Matthew 25:24|Mt 25:24⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of things, ⟪hard, rough, violent⟫: σκληρόν σοι (ἐστι), ⟦Acts 26:14|Ac 26:14⟧; λόγος, ⟦John 6:60|Jo 6:60⟧; ἄνεμος, ⟦James 3:4|Ja 3:4⟧; σκληρὰ λαλεῖν, ⟦Jude 1:15|Ju 15⟧.†
SYN.: αὐστηρός, q.v

G4678.b:
⟪σοφία⟫, -ας, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨חׇכְמָה⁩ ;] ⟪skill, intelligence, wisdom⟫, ranging from knowledge of the arts and matters of daily life to mental excellence in its highest and fullest sense;
⟪(a)⟫ of human wisdom: ⟦1 Corinthians 2:1|I Co 2:1⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:4|4, 5⟧, ⟦James 3:15|Ja 3:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:18|Re 13:18⟧ ⟦Revelation 17:9|17:9⟧; σ. Σολομῶνος, ⟦Matthew 12:42|Mt 12:42⟧, ⟦Luke 11:31|Lk 11:31⟧; Αἰγυπτίων, ⟦Acts 7:22|Ac 7:22⟧; Ἕλληνες σ. ζητοῦσιν, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:22|I Co 1:22⟧; σ. λόγου, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:17|I Co 1:17⟧; τ. σοφῶν, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:19|ib. 19⟧ (LXX); τ. κόσμου, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:20|ib. 20, 21⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 3:19|3:19⟧; ἀνθρωπίνη, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:13|I Co 2:13⟧; σαρκική, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:12|II Co 1:12⟧; of wisdom in spiritual things: ⟦Luke 21:15|Lk 21:15⟧, ⟦Acts 6:3|Ac 6:3⟧, ⟦Acts 6:10|10⟧ ⟦Acts 7:10|7:10⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:6|I Co 2:6⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:28|Col 1:28⟧ ⟦Colossians 2:23|2:23⟧ ⟦Colossians 3:16|3:16⟧ ⟦Colossians 4:5|4:5⟧, ⟦James 1:5|Ja 1:5⟧ ⟦James 3:13|3:13⟧, ⟦James 3:17|17⟧, ⟦2 Peter 3:15|II Pe 3:15⟧; λόγος σοφίας, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:8|I Co 12:8⟧; πνεῦμα σοφίας, ⟦Ephesians 1:17|Eph 1:17⟧; σ. καὶ φρόνησις, ⟦Ephesians 1:8|Eph 1:8⟧; σ. καὶ σύνεσις, ⟦Colossians 1:9|Col 1:9⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of divine wisdom: of God, ⟦Romans 11:33|Ro 11:33⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:21|I Co 1:21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:24|24⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 2:7|2:7⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:12|Re 7:12⟧; πολυποίκιλος, ⟦Ephesians 3:10|Eph 3:10⟧ of Christ, ⟦Matthew 13:54|Mt 13:54⟧, ⟦Mark 6:2|Mk 6:2⟧, ⟦Luke 2:40|Lk 2:40⟧, ⟦Luke 2:52|52⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:30|I Co 1:30⟧ ⟦Colossians 2:3|Col 2:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:12|Re 5:12⟧; of wisdom personified, ⟦Matthew 11:19|Mt 11:19⟧, ⟦Luke 7:35|Lk 7:35⟧ ⟦Luke 11:49|11:49⟧.†
SYN.: σύνεσις, ⟪intelligence⟫; φρόνησις, ⟪prudence⟫, which with σ. make up (Arist., N. Eth., i, 13) the three intellectual ἀρεταί. σ. is ⟪wisdom⟫ primary and absolute; in distinction from which φ. is practical, σύνεσις critical, both being applications of σ. in detail (cf. Lft., and ICC on ⟦Colossians 1:9|Col 1:9⟧; Lft., Notes, 317 f.; Tr., Syn., § lxxv; Cremer, 870 ff.).

G4679.b:
⟪σοφίζω⟫
(< σοφός), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨חכם⁩ ;] ⟪to make wise, instruct⟫: c. acc. pers., ⟦2 Timothy 3:15|II Ti 3:15⟧ (cf. ⟦Psalms 19:8|Ps 18 (19):8⟧ (⟦Psalms 119:98|Ps 118 (119):98⟧). As depon., -ομαι;
⟪(a)⟫ intrans., ⟪to become wise⟫ (⟦1 Kings 5:11|III Ki 4:27 ( 5:11)⟧), ⟦Ecclesiastes 2:15|Ec 2:15⟧, and freq. in Si 7:5, al.);
⟪(b)⟫ trans., ⟪to invent, devise cleverly⟫: pass., ⟦2 Peter 1:16|II Pe 1:16⟧ (cf. κατα-σοφίζομαι).†

G4690.b:
⟪σπέρμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< σπείρω) [in LXX chiefly for ⁨זֶרַע⁩ ;] ⟪seed⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of plants: ⟦Matthew 13:24|Mt 13:24⟧, ⟦Matthew 13:27|27⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:37|37, 38⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 9:10|II Co 9:10⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 13:32|Mt 13:32⟧, ⟦Mark 4:31|Mk 4:31⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:33|I Co 15:33⟧; metaph., of an escaping remnant (⁨שָׂרִיד⁩, ⟦Isaiah 1:9|Is 1:9⟧; cf. Wi 14:6; Plat., Tim., 23 c; FlJ, Ant., xi, 5, 3), ⟦Romans 9:29|Ro 9:29⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of men (as γονή; Lat. semen genitale; so in cl.; cf. in LXX, ⟦Leviticus 15:16|Le 15:16⟧, al.): ⟦Hebrews 11:11|He 11:11⟧; metaph., of the divine influence, ⟦1 John 3:9|I Jo 3:9⟧; by meton. (as freq. in poets), ⟪seed, offspring, posterity⟫: ⟦Matthew 22:24|Mt 22:24, 25⟧, ⟦Mark 12:19|Mk 12:19-22⟧, ⟦Luke 1:55|Lk 1:55⟧ ⟦Luke 20:28|20:28⟧ (LXX) ⟦John 7:42|Jo 7:42⟧ ⟦John 8:33|8:33⟧, ⟦John 8:37|37⟧ ⟦Acts 3:25|Ac 3:25⟧ ⟦Acts 7:5|7:5, 6⟧ ⟦Acts 13:23|13:23⟧, ⟦Romans 1:3|Ro 1:3⟧ ⟦Romans 4:13|4:13⟧, ⟦Romans 4:18|18⟧ ⟦Romans 9:7|9:7, 8⟧ ⟦Romans 11:1|11:1⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:22|II Co 11:22⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:16|Ga 3:16⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:19|19⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:8|II Ti 2:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:16|He 2:16⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:18|11:18⟧; pl. (FlJ, Ant., viii, 7, 6; Plat., Leg., ix, 853 c; IV Mac 18:1; in Ga, l.c., contrasted with sing., v. Lft., in l; Milligan, NTD, 105 f.), ⟦Galatians 3:16|Ga 3:16⟧; of spiritual offspring, ⟦Romans 4:16|Ro 4:16⟧, ⟦Romans 4:18|18⟧ ⟦Romans 9:8|9:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:29|Ga 3:29⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:17|Re 12:17⟧.†

G4691.b:
* ⟪σπερμολόγος⟫, -ον
(< σπέρμα, λέγω) ⟪a seed picker⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ prop., of birds (Arist., Aristoph, al.);
⟪(b)⟫ in Attic slang, of an idler who lives on scraps picked up in the agora; hence, as subst., ὁ σ., ⟪an idle babbler⟫: ⟦Acts 17:18|Ac 17:18⟧.†

G4692.b:
⟪σπεύδω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨מהר⁩ pi., also for ⁨בּהל⁩ pi., hi., etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ most freq. intrans., ⟪to hasten⟫: c. inf. (as freq. in cl.), ⟦Acts 20:16|Ac 20:16⟧; ptcp. c. indic., ⟦Luke 2:16|Lk 2:16⟧; c. imperat., ⟦Luke 19:5|Lk 19:5, 6⟧; σπεῦσον κ. ἔξελθε, ⟦Acts 22:18|Ac 22:18⟧
⟪2.⟫ Trans., c. acc;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to hasten, urge on, accelerate⟫ (as Hom., Od., xix, 137; Eur., Med., 152; Si 33(36):8): ⟦2 Peter 3:12|II Pe 3:12⟧, R, mg. (cf. Mayor and ICC, in l., but v. infr.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to desire eagerly⟫ (Pind., Pyth., iii, 110; Eur., Suppl., 161; ⟦Isaiah 16:5|Is 16:5⟧): ⟦2 Peter 3:12|II Pe, l.c.⟧, R, txt. (but v. supr.).†
